# 4️⃣ Queue Reconstruction by Height

## 📖 Problem

Each person:

```text
[h, k]
```

where:

```text
h = height
k = people in front
with height >= h
```

Reconstruct the queue.

---

### Example

```text
[7,0]
[4,4]
[7,1]
[5,0]
[6,1]
[5,2]
```

---

# 5️⃣ Greedy Strategy

Sort:

```text
Height Descending
```

If heights equal:

```text
k Ascending
```

Then insert each person at index k.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<vector<int>>
reconstructQueue(
vector<vector<int>>& people)
{
    sort(
        people.begin(),
        people.end(),
        [](auto &a, auto &b)
        {
            if(a[0] == b[0])
                return a[1] < b[1];

            return a[0] > b[0];
        }
    );

    vector<vector<int>> answer;

    for(auto &person : people)
    {
        answer.insert(
            answer.begin() +
            person[1],
            person
        );
    }

    return answer;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N²)

Space: O(N)
```

