# 🔟 Minimum Refueling Stops

## 📖 Problem

Reach target distance.

You start with:

```text
Fuel
```

There are fuel stations.

Find minimum refueling stops.

---

### Example

```text
Target = 100

Fuel = 10
```

Stations:

```text
10 60
20 30
30 30
60 40
```

Output:

```text
2
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Greedy Strategy

Whenever fuel becomes insufficient:

```text
Refuel from largest station
already passed.
```

Use:

```text
Max Heap
```

---

### Why?

Largest fuel gives maximum reach.

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N log N)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Course Schedule III

## 📖 Problem

Each course:

```text
Duration
Deadline
```

Take maximum number of courses.

---

### Example

```text
[100,200]
[200,1300]
[1000,1250]
[2000,3200]
```

Output:

```text
3
```

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ Greedy Strategy

Sort by:

```text
Deadline
```

Take courses one by one.

Maintain:

```text
Total Time
```

If total time exceeds deadline:

```text
Remove
Longest Duration Course
```

Use:

```text
Max Heap
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N log N)

Space: O(N)
```

